## Baking soda
component-sodium-bicarbonate = Baking soda
    .genitive = baking soda
component-sodium-bicarbonate-decomposes-into = washing soda (Na₂CO₃), water and carbon dioxide
component-sodium-bicarbonate-description-novice = A white powder found in every kitchen. With vinegar it fizzes violently, giving off carbon dioxide. That is why soda makes dough rise.
component-sodium-bicarbonate-description-school = Sodium hydrogen carbonate NaHCO₃ starts to decompose from ≈ 50 °C into Na₂CO₃, water and CO₂. With acids (acetic, citric) it reacts, releasing CO₂.
component-sodium-bicarbonate-safety-school = Irritates the eyes — keep it out of your eyes.
component-sodium-bicarbonate-model-notes = The engine does not compute chemical reactions (soda + vinegar) yet.
component-sodium-bicarbonate-model-notes-2 = The enthalpy of solution is not checked against sources yet, so in the model dissolving does not change the temperature.
